    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d483-a5">

                <pb facs="0566" n="486" sameAs="frus:frus1902/pg486"/>

                <opener><seg rendition="#center">[Inclosure 4.]</seg></opener>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">Mr. Hay to Mr.
                            Naphen.</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Department of State</hi>,<lb/><hi rendition="#italic"
                                >Washington</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1902-02-25"><hi rendition="#italic">February 25,
                        1902</hi></date>.</dateline></opener>
                <p><hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: Referring to your letter of January 16
                    last, in regard to James L. Molloy, a prisoner of war at Hamilton, Bermuda, I
                    have the honor to inclose copy of a dispatch<anchor n="b" xml:id="d483-f1"/>
                    from the consul at Hamilton reporting that Mr. Molloy is in the hospital, but
                    will be able to leave it in a few weeks.</p>
                <p>I have, etc.,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">John Hay.</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
